LLM Training
Experimental implementations and experiments by Naveen Kannan.

The work originated in Stanford CS336 and is organized here by subsystem.
Original course handouts, assignment write-ups, tests, datasets, credentials,
and grading/submission infrastructure are not part of this distribution.

MIT-licensed Stanford sources:
  https://github.com/stanford-cs336/assignment1-basics
  https://github.com/stanford-cs336/assignment2-systems
  https://github.com/stanford-cs336/assignment3-scaling
  https://github.com/stanford-cs336/assignment4-data

src/llm_training/pretraining contains Naveen's tokenizer, model, optimizer,
and training implementations, developed against Stanford scaffolding.
src/llm_training/systems contains experimental attention, distributed
training, and profiling implementations and benchmark scaffolding.
src/llm_training/reference is Stanford's reference transformer implementation,
used by systems benchmarks; it is not presented as Naveen's own implementation.
src/llm_training/data contains data-processing experiments and supporting
scaffolding. The scaling reference curves are upstream provided data, not
measurements from Naveen's own training runs.

src/llm_training/posttraining contains custom GRPO utilities and experiment
runners. Upstream loader/server/prompt assets without a license in the
inspected source snapshot are intentionally not redistributed.

